v3.2.5

Summary
- Bug fix release. Resolves an event loop busy-loop on loop mode, orphaned audio player tasks after $leave, an unguarded JSON decode in oEmbed resolution, a broken embed uploader link, and a Groq fallback bypass during Gemini quota exhaustion.

🔧 BUG FIX: EVENT LOOP BUSY-LOOP
- FIXED: When $loop was enabled and no track was set (e.g. after a playback error), audio_player_task entered a tight CPU-spinning busy-loop with no await point, stalling the entire bot event loop.
- Added await asyncio.sleep(0) before continue to yield control back to the event loop in this code path.

🔧 BUG FIX: ORPHANED AUDIO PLAYER TASK
- FIXED: $leave ($disconnect) called VoiceState.stop() which disconnected voice and cleared the queue but never cancelled the audio_player asyncio task.
- The orphaned task remained alive, blocking on a 180s idle timeout, holding a reference to the old VoiceState and preventing garbage collection. Repeated $leave/$join cycles accumulated zombie tasks.
- stop() now explicitly cancels audio_player and sets current = None before disconnecting.

🔧 BUG FIX: OEMBED JSON DECODE CRASH
- FIXED: _fetch_oembed_metadata() called json.loads() without a try/except. A non-JSON response (e.g. an HTML error page from a Spotify or Apple Music oEmbed endpoint) would raise an unhandled json.JSONDecodeError, crashing $play for those link types.
- json.loads() is now guarded and raises a clear ValueError on decode failure, which is caught cleanly by the caller.

🔧 BUG FIX: BROKEN UPLOADER EMBED LINK
- FIXED: Song.create_embed() built the Uploader field as [{uploader}]({uploader_url}) without null-checking uploader_url. When uploader_url was absent (common for some extractors), Discord rendered a literal [None](None) broken hyperlink.
- Uploader field now renders as a plain name when URL is absent, and falls back to "Unknown" when uploader name is also missing.

🔧 BUG FIX: GROQ FALLBACK BYPASSED DURING GEMINI QUOTA
- FIXED: _ai_quota_check() returned True during Gemini quota exhaustion and immediately sent BARD_QUOTA_MESSAGE, bypassing Groq entirely — even when a working Groq client was configured.
- $ask, $bard, and $roastdj now only gate on quota exhaustion when Groq is also unavailable. If _groq_client is set, requests proceed and generate_content() routes to Groq as intended.

v3.2.4

Summary
- AI persona overhaul: tighter Biden-isms, less verbosity, more authentic voice. Fixed YouTube single-video playlist extraction bug. Removed redundant $dj command.

🤖 AI PERSONA UPDATE
- Rewrote AI persona for tighter, more authentic Biden voice.
- Word limit reduced: 400 words → 150 words (no more novels).
- Lean into folksy Biden-isms: "Look, here's the deal," "Not a joke," "No malarkey," "C'mon, man."
- When recommending songs, AI now outputs cleaner QUEUE_SONGS format.

🔧 BUG FIX: YOUTUBE PLAYLIST EXTRACTION
- FIXED: Certain YouTube URLs (e.g., youtu.be with si= tracking param) intermittently queued up to 50 songs.
- Root cause: 'extract_flat': 'in_playlist' in YTDL_OPTIONS conflicted with 'noplaylist': True.
- Removed extract_flat from YTDL_OPTIONS — single-video extraction now properly isolated.
- Playlist functionality preserved via YTDL_PLAYLIST_OPTIONS.

🧹 CLEANUP
- REMOVED: $dj command (redundant with $bard, which also queues songs via QUEUE_SONGS).
- Updated $help and $usage menus to remove $dj references.

🎵 PLAYLIST LIMIT REDUCED
- Playlist import limit: 50 tracks → 25 tracks.
- Users can still queue unlimited songs individually; only playlist bulk-import is capped.

🔊 DEFAULT VOLUME CHANGE
- Default volume on channel join: 50% → 100%.
- Users can still adjust with $volume 0-100 as needed.

v3.2.3

Summary
- Production promotion of the v3.2.3 Beta build. Integrates Groq (Llama/Mixtral) as a cross-provider AI fallback, hardens security, and fixes a critical bot startup defect. All beta references removed.

🤖 NEW: GROQ AI FALLBACK
- Added generate_content_with_groq() and a top-level generate_content() dispatcher.
- All AI commands ($ask, $bard, $roastdj) now route through generate_content(), which tries Gemini first and falls through to Groq only on full Gemini failure (outage, key issues, all models exhausted).
- Groq quota errors do NOT trigger fallback — daily quota exhaustion still surfaces the BARD_QUOTA_MESSAGE correctly.
- Groq models tried in order: llama-3.3-70b-versatile → llama-3.1-8b-instant → mixtral-8x7b-32768.
- Groq is optional: set GROQ_API_KEY in .env to enable. If absent, bot warns at startup and skips Groq silently.
- Free Groq key: https://console.groq.com — email signup, no billing, ~60 seconds. Difficulty: 1/5.
- AI availability guards updated across all commands to check both Gemini and Groq, not just Gemini.
- openai>=1.0.0 added to requirements.txt (used as the Groq API compatibility layer).

🔧 CRITICAL FIX: BOT STARTUP
- FIXED: bot.run(token) was missing from the Beta source — bot would import successfully but never start. Added.

🔒 SECURITY
- FIXED: _roastdj now sanitizes roast_target.display_name through _sanitize_ai_input() before embedding in AI prompt. Prevents user-controlled display names from being used as prompt injection vectors.
- REMOVED: Unknown package 'davey' from requirements.txt (no code references; potential typosquat risk).

🔁 AI MODEL SELECTION (carried from Beta)
- Replaced deprecated get_best_available_model() / client.models.list() call (removed in google-genai SDK 1.0+) with a hardcoded preferred-model list validated asynchronously in on_ready.
- Models probed in order: gemini-2.5-flash → gemini-1.5-flash → gemini-1.5-pro → gemini-2.0-flash.

🎛️ INTENTS HARDENING
- Replaced discord.Intents.all() (over-permissioned) with a minimal explicit intent set: guilds, voice_states, guild_messages, message_content, members.

v3.0

Summary
- Production release incorporating all beta-tested fixes. Resolves the critical "enqueued but nothing plays" idle bug, reworks FFmpeg process management, adds stream URL re-resolution, and improves state cleanup on disconnect.

🔧 CRITICAL FIX: STALE PLAYBACK BUG
- FIXED: Songs would enqueue but never play after the bot sat idle for ~3 minutes. Root cause: the internal audio player task died on idle timeout but the bot kept reusing the dead session. New songs went into a queue nobody was consuming.
- FIXED: "Already playing audio" errors caused by stale voice client state after Discord voice reconnects. The bot now force-clears any stuck player before starting a new track.
- FIXED: Redundant manual ffmpeg process tracking that conflicted with discord.py's own cleanup — caused the "ffmpeg process should have terminated with return code of -9" log spam and potential double-termination issues. Removed entirely; discord.py manages ffmpeg lifecycle internally.
- Added voice connection health check (is_connected) before attempting playback.
- Added stream URL re-resolution at play time to avoid stale/expired YouTube URLs.
- Added diagnostic logging throughout the player lifecycle for easier future debugging.

🔁 REWORKED: LOOP COMMAND
- $loop now requires on/off flag ($loop on / $loop off) — consistent with all other effect commands.
- $stop now explicitly disables loop, so loop can no longer override a stop command.
- Loop state is displayed with a clear text message instead of just a reaction.

🧹 STATE CLEANUP ON DISCONNECT
- All effect and loop states are now reset when the bot disconnects — whether via $leave, $stop, or idle timeout.
- New internal _reset_effects() helper ensures loop, nightcore, slowmo, vaporwave, reverse, bass, lofi, echo, tremolo, and fadein are all cleared to defaults on disconnect.
- Prevents stale effect settings from carrying over into the next listening session.

📋 UPDATED HELP
- Help menu updated to show $loop on|off syntax.

v2.4

Bugfixes
- Removed references to the old bot name

Summary
- Major update with AI integration, advanced audio effects, FFmpeg fixes, and command prefix change. This is the biggest feature update yet!

🤖 NEW: AI INTEGRATION
- Added Google Gemini AI integration with free tier support (1,500 requests/day)
- Added $ask command for general Q&A with context awareness
- Added $dj command for music recommendations and DJ assistance
- Added $chat command for private AI conversations in DMs
- Added $aistats command to monitor AI usage and limits
- AI is music-aware - knows current song, queue, and active effects
- Built-in rate limiting and usage tracking to prevent abuse
- Smart error handling for API failures and rate limits

🎛️ NEW: ADVANCED AUDIO EFFECTS
- Added $slowmo on/off - Slow down music by 15% (opposite of nightcore)
- Added $vaporwave on/off - Aesthetic slowed + echo effect
- Added $reverse on/off - Play music backwards for party tricks
- Added $bass on/off - Heavy bass boost for party vibes
- Added $lofi on/off - Crunchy vintage lo-fi sound for study sessions
- Added $echo on/off - Triple echo chamber for atmospheric effects
- Added $tremolo on/off - Pulsing tremolo effect for rave vibes
- Added $fadein on/off - Smooth fade-in for professional transitions
- Added $effects command to show all available effects and status
- Only one effect can be active at a time (auto-switching)
- Enhanced FFmpeg options with timeout protection (50 minutes)
- All effects use professional-grade FFmpeg audio filters
- REMOVED: $robot effect (had technical issues)

🔧 CRITICAL FIXES
- FIXED: FFmpeg termination errors that caused bot to become unresponsive
- FIXED: "failed to terminate -9" errors with proper process cleanup
- FIXED: Memory leaks from unclosed FFmpeg processes
- Added thread-safe cleanup with asyncio.Lock()
- Enhanced error handling for audio playback failures
- Improved process termination with graceful fallbacks

💫 QUALITY IMPROVEMENTS
- Changed command prefix from ! to $ as requested
- Fixed duplicate asyncio import in code
- Fixed missing duration_seconds attribute (broke $nowbar command)
- Improved cog_unload method with proper async handling
- Enhanced error handling throughout the codebase
- Optimized imports and removed redundancies

📚 UPDATED DOCUMENTATION
- Completely rewritten README.md with comprehensive feature guide
- Updated requirements.txt to include google-generativeai
- Added detailed audio effects guide with use cases
- Added AI features documentation with examples
- Enhanced troubleshooting section
- Added party mode ideas and configuration guide

🎮 ENHANCED USER EXPERIENCE
- Updated $usage command to include AI features
- Added AI commands to $help menu
- Enhanced $effects command with party tips
- Improved error messages and user feedback
- Better organization of command categories

🔒 PRODUCTION READY
- Comprehensive error handling and recovery
- Rate limiting and abuse prevention
- Memory leak prevention
- Thread-safe operations
- Graceful shutdown handling
- Extensive testing and validation

v2.3 (Previous Version)

Summary
- Feature expansion update with new interactive music commands, playlist persistence, and richer playback controls.

New Features
- Added a custom embedded `!help` command menu grouped by Music, Playback Controls, Playlists, and Utility commands.
- Added !lyrics for lyric lookup (artist - title format).
- Added !nightcore on|off for a nightcore playback effect on upcoming tracks.
- Added !replay to restart the current track quickly.
- Added !history to show recently played tracks.
- Added !playlist save/load/list with per-server JSON persistence.
- Added !votemode on|off (alias: !vote) for vote-based skipping.
- Added !mood happy|chill|rage|focus to queue mood-based presets.
- Added !roastdj to roast current DJ or a tagged member.
- Added !stats for uptime and playback metrics.
- Added !nowbar for a live progress bar display.
- Expanded command docstrings so !help clearly explains usage and aliases.

Fixes
- Fixed environment load order so .env values are applied before MUSIC_CHANNEL_ID parsing.
- Fixed playback source handling to preserve track metadata while still refreshing stream sources.
- Fixed occasional volume command edge cases when voice source is missing.
- Fixed patchnotes loading path so !patchnotes works even if bot is launched from a different directory.
- Added explicit startup error when DISCORD_TOKEN is missing.

Behavior and Reliability Improvements
- Improved audio player loop safety checks and vote reset behavior per track.
- Simplified on_message branching to reduce duplicated checks and unnecessary random emoji work.
- Added stronger type guards/casts to reduce false-positive analyzer warnings in editor.
- Added playback history tracking and per-track start time tracking for richer command output.
- Added playlist read/write helpers and safer JSON fallback behavior.

Notes
- !play_spotify remains a placeholder command and is not direct Spotify playback.
- If imports show unresolved in editor, install dependencies in the active venv:
	discord.py, yt-dlp, python-dotenv

Bugs
- None known at release time. Report new issues in Discord with command used and error output.
